--TEST--
A parameter with no `@param` line, where the comment documents another parameter, is warning `W1030`, and the line its fix inserts is `E0139` until it has a sentence — `rule:tooling/doc-comment-tags-are-closed-and-checked`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Once a comment has one `@param` line, each parameter has one.
// `add` is warned about `$note`. `sum` has no `@param` line, so it is not warned.
// `take` shows the line the fix inserts, before its sentence is written.
final class Ledger {
    /// Adds one entry.
    ///
    /// @param $amount the amount to add
    public static function add(int $amount, string $note): int {
        return $amount;
    }

    /// Adds two amounts.
    public static function sum(int $a, int $b): int {
        return $a + $b;
    }

    /// Takes one entry away.
    ///
    /// @param $amount the amount to take away
    /// @param $note
    public static function take(int $amount, string $note): int {
        return -$amount;
    }
}
echo Ledger::add(3, "x"), "\n";
echo Ledger::sum(1, 2), "\n";
echo Ledger::take(1, "y"), "\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
warning[W1030]: `$note` has no `@param` line
  --> %s:9:52
  |
9 |     public static function add(int $amount, string $note): int {
  |                                                    ^^^^^ the other parameters have one
  = suggestion: add an `@param $note` line

error[E0139]: `@param $note` has no text
   --> %s:21:9
   |
21 |     /// @param $note
   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^ write what `$note` means

error: aborting due to 1 error; 1 warning emitted
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
